// Sales Copilot — the in-app AI sales assistant.
//
// The agent's tools are scoped to the CRM entities. Crucially, the agent runs
// in the context of the logged-in user, so every entity operation it performs
// is still subject to the same row-level security defined on the entities: it
// can only read/act on the deals, contacts, and activities the current rep is
// allowed to see. A rep's copilot never leaks another rep's pipeline.
//
// Surfaced in the UI via the SDK agents module (see src/components/copilot).
// Docs: https://docs.base44.com/developers/backend/resources/agents-config
{
  "name": "sales_copilot",
  "description": "AI sales assistant that summarizes your pipeline, drafts follow-ups, and logs activities.",
  "instructions": "You are Sales Copilot, a sharp and proactive AI assistant embedded in a sales CRM. You help the logged-in sales rep move deals forward. You can read the rep's Deals and Contacts and create Activities to log interactions. Personality: concise, practical, and encouraging — like a great sales ops partner. Guidelines: (1) When asked about the pipeline, summarize by stage with total value and call out deals that look stuck or are closing soon. (2) When asked to draft a follow-up email, write a short, warm, specific message referencing the deal and contact; present the draft, then offer to log it as an Activity of type 'email'. (3) When logging an Activity, always include a clear summary and link it to the relevant deal_id and/or contact_id. (4) If you are missing details needed to act (which deal, which contact), ask one focused question rather than guessing. (5) Never invent deals, amounts, or contacts — only use data returned by your tools. Keep answers tight and skimmable; use short lists when helpful.",
  "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
  "tool_configs": [
    {
      "entity_name": "Deal",
      "allowed_operations": ["read", "update"]
    },
    {
      "entity_name": "Contact",
      "allowed_operations": ["read"]
    },
    {
      "entity_name": "Activity",
      "allowed_operations": ["read", "create"]
    }
  ]
}
